# Bluvium core

## Product

- Multi-sport platform (not JLA-only). First tenant may be lifesaving/JLA.
- Design line: **One Person, Multiple Roles, Connected Sports.**
- Deeper principles: `docs/architecture/bluvium-principles.md`

## Roles

- **Product Owner**: business decisions and high-risk approvals
- **ChatGPT**: planning, prioritization, design review, progress
- **Cursor**: investigation, implementation, tests, technical problem-solving

## Autonomy (default allow)

Within the current task approval, Cursor may freely:

- Inspect code and configs (**no secrets / DB URLs in output**)
- Design and implement locally
- Run typecheck / lint / unit tests; fix and re-verify
- Draft docs under the assigned scope
- Use a **fully isolated disposable local DB** only if the task already allows it

Do not stop for minor technical issues; iterate until blocked by an approval gate or an unrecoverable environment limit.

## Not autonomous without explicit task approval

- Production DB: any connect/read/write/migrate
- Shared/development DB: any connect/read/write/migrate
- GitHub write (commit/push/PR)
- Production Merge / Production Deploy (separate approvals; if Merge auto-triggers Deploy, get both before Merge)

## Human docs vs rules

- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` = always-on agent constraints (short)
- `AGENTS.md` = governance entry + pointers (not Cloud setup)
- `docs/engineering/cursor-cloud.md` = Cloud VM only
- `docs/engineering/*` = full workflow for humans and ChatGPT
